## The library inside this jar

night-config (`core` and `toml`), by TheElectronWill, is the TOML reader and writer behind Anima's
config files. It rides nested at `META-INF/jars/`, unmodified, exactly as published to Maven
Central: https://github.com/TheElectronWill/night-config

It is LGPL-3.0, and its own jars carry no licence text — so `licenses/LGPL-3.0.txt` and
`licenses/GPL-3.0.txt` in this jar are the only place a holder of this file can read its terms.
Both texts, because the LGPL is not a whole licence: it is additional permissions written on top of
the GPL, and one without the other conveys nothing.

Replacing it is meant to work. Drop a newer night-config into `mods/` and Fabric Loader prefers it
over the copy nested here; nothing is shaded or relocated, so nothing needs recompiling.

## About the name

"Anima" is Latin — soul, breath, the thing that animates. It is an old word and I did not invent
it, but the association between that name and this library is mine, as is the mod id `anima` that
identifies it to the game. Neither is covered by the Apache licence: the licence is about code, and
says nothing about naming.

Fork freely, rename before you publish or clearly state it's a fork. Let me know if you do, I'd love
to see other people's work on it.
